# Survey – generated by the "question-me" skill

## Round 1

```survey-json
{
  "round": 1,
  "generatedAt": "2026-11-23T08:14:22.000Z",
  "stage": "stage-1792362077711",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "The runners update themselves gradually when idle (the backend nudges them at most once a day each; nobody force-restarts them). For that to happen, the backend must be set to 'recommend' runner version 0.2.x. Is that recommendation already switched on — so this task only watches and records — or should the backend setting also be checked (and switched on if missing)?",
      "options": [
        "It is already set — this task only observes and records versions before/after (Recommended)",
        "Check it, and if 0.2.x is not recommended yet, switch the recommendation on (a small backend config change, no restarts)",
        "Do not touch the backend at all; only use what is already recorded in the repo docs"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Verifying the rollout needs read-only peeks at the live system: asking the backend which runner versions are running and re-reading task histories, plus reading runner logs and leftover task work folders (kb-<taskId> worktrees) on both runner machines. You previously approved read-only prod log access for a related investigation. Does that approval also cover these read-only checks for this task? Nothing will be restarted, deleted, force-updated, or re-run.",
      "options": [
        "Yes — read-only access to the backend API, runner logs, and work folders is approved for this task too (Recommended)",
        "Only backend API reads (versions + task histories); no runner-host log or worktree access",
        "No live access at all — rely only on what is already recorded in the repo docs"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "Runners only update when idle, at most once a day each, so the two named runners (local-alpha, server2-alpha) may take hours or longer to reach 0.2.x. How should this task handle the wait?",
      "options": [
        "Wait and watch until both local-alpha and server2-alpha run a 0.2.x build, then do the 'after' recount in the same run (Recommended)",
        "Record the 'before' numbers now and stop; do the 'after' recount in a later run once convergence is confirmed",
        "Do not wait — record before/after whenever convenient, even if the runners are still mid-rollout"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "single",
      "text": "The original interruption survey counted one project (61 tasks). For the before/after interrupt recount, which scope do you want?",
      "options": [
        "The same project only, so the numbers compare directly with the 2026-11-21 baseline (Recommended)",
        "All projects on the backend (whole fleet)",
        "The same project plus any other project that shows interruptions"
      ],
      "required": true,
      "showIf": null
    }
  ],
  "answers": {
    "q1": {
      "selected": [
        "It is already set — this task only observes and records versions before/after (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q2": {
      "selected": [
        "Yes — read-only access to the backend API, runner logs, and work folders is approved for this task too (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q3": {
      "selected": [
        "Wait and watch until both local-alpha and server2-alpha run a 0.2.x build, then do the 'after' recount in the same run (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    },
    "q4": {
      "selected": [
        "The same project only, so the numbers compare directly with the 2026-11-21 baseline (Recommended)"
      ],
      "notes": ""
    }
  }
}
```

